#33 isn't landed yet: the fix is committed and queued with the manager, but no build has been able to run its gates. The issue is now marked `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#113`, which ends this run.

- **The change:** commit 2efb74d adds `security-exceptions.yaml` at the repository root with exactly the seven ids from #27 to #33. Each entry has the triage's reason, `decided_by: "hub (Jody's delegation, 2026-11-10)"` and `expires: 2027-02-10`. No path is allowlisted, and STATE.md and PROPOSALS.md are updated. It is the previous run's work, committed again on main a43bc79.
- **What I checked:** the seven ids match the findings in #27 to #33 exactly, and the entries follow the form in the looper README (four keys, no others). I could not parse the YAML, because this machine has no yaml module and no ruby. `looper-trace check` passes with 0 handlers; no handler was touched.
- **Why the last land failed:** the build infrastructure, not the change. Its build (pipeline 3052873919) gave no verdict in 3h. The build I requested this run (pipeline 3053342983) set no commit status in 20 minutes. Lands and builds for #25, #56, opa#9 and gateway#29 stalled the same way, which is what tacplus-dev/looper#113 tracks. No gate run has finished, so I have none to report.
- **The land:** queued again at 08:29Z on the full gates. The manager merges it only if they pass and posts its verdict on #33. I stopped my local wait on it; the land stays in the manager's queue.
- **Still red after it lands:** main's security job will probably still fail. The cargo-deny "unlicensed" findings #34 to #55 are blocking too, and they wait on tacplus-dev/tacplus#368 and #390.
- **Backport:** pull request #57 against release/0.1 is open and its GitHub `gates` check passes. Once it merges, the patch is tagged on release/0.1: `v0.1.7`, or `v0.1.8` if #26 takes `v0.1.7` first. No patch is tagged from main, because main already carries #13, which belongs to the next minor.

Everything is in a progress comment on #33. The next run, after #113 closes, confirms the land, tags the patch and closes the issue.
